WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.600
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский, episode 61, for 18 июля 2026 года, I am

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.000
Olya.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.300
Today's lesson is going to be a fun one.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.080
Поехали!

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.980
Today our word is magazine, magazine.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.600
It sounds like magazine, but it means the place where you buy things.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.820
Я иду в магазин, я иду в магазин, means I am going to the store.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.820
Can you say it with me, magazine?

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.920
Надо чуно у магазин, let's learn more words for shopping.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.340
The first is to buy, купит, купит it means to buy.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.880
Я хочу купить хлеб, я хочу купить хлеб, means I want to buy bread,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.480
repeat after me, купить.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.380
Next comes деньги, где еде.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.660
У меня есть деньги, и меня есть деньги, means I have money.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:54.140
Remember fruit from a few lessons ago, you need money to buy them.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.420
Let's keep building, довор цена, means price.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.940
Цена, какая цена, какая цена, means what is the price, repeat after me.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.160
Цена, на утра сумка, сумка, сумка, means bag.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.300
У меня большая сумка, у меня большая сумка, means I have a big bag.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.360
It helps when you carry lots of things from the magazine.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.320
Next is платить, платит, платит, means to pay.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.120
Я плачу за молоко, я плачу за молоко, means I pay for the milk.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.060
Repeat after me, платит.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:32.700
The person who helps you is продовец, продовец, продовец, means seller or shop assistant.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:38.680
Продовец помогает мне, продовец помогает мне, means the seller helps me.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.140
Our last two words connect nicely.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.680
Карзина из баскет оркарт, корзина, положи фрукты в корзину,

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.900
положи фрукты в корзину, means put the fruit in the basket.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.700
И скидка, means discount, скидка, есть скидка на этот товар,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.080
есть скидка на этот товар, means there is discount on this item.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:04.320
Now for a quick grammar bite, the work-cupid changes depending on who is doing the action.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:09.920
We say я куплю, for I will buy, я куплю you, ты купишь, for you will buy,

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.220
ты купишь, он купит, она купит,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.260
for he or she will buy, он купишь,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.600
а он купишь.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.060
The ending of the work tells us who is acting,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.940
unlike English, where we often keep the same form.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:27.000
In Russia, many people still love outdoor markets called рынок.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.640
There they buy fresh fruits and vegetables of directly from farmers.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.920
These places are lively, with friendly bargaining and tasting samples.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.420
Shopping becomes a social event full of smiles and conversations.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.680
Let's practice what we learned.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.020
Do you remember what magazine means?

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.900
Try saying it out loud now.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:50.620
For kids, draw a big shopping basket and feed it with pictures while saying each Russian word.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.020
For adults, next time you see a price tag, practice сколько стоит,

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.220
how much does it cost?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.800
Now here's something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.300
Want to know a secret about magazine?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.220
Did you know that the Russian word magazine and the English word magazine

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.640
are actually the same word?

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:12.200
They both come from the Arabic magazine, meaning storehouses or shops.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.740
This word started in Arabic, travel through Italian and French as magazine,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.960
and finally arrived in Russian in the 19th century.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.000
But be careful, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.740
But actually means shop.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.680
Next time you see a magazine on a shelf, remember.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.640
It has cousins with magazine.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.120
They both come from the same Arabic root for storing goods.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.920
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.420
You did great today.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.860
Say today's words out loud one more time and there yours.

